    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file when run through the frai CLI wrapper.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main `frai` command's option parser and not passed through to the spawned `frai-gate` process. In commander.js, global options on the main command aren't automatically forwarded to subcommands.\n\n### The Fix\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-756):\n- Changed the gate command's action handler to check if `--ci` is present in `process.argv`\n- If found, add it to the arguments passed to the frai-gate CLI\n\nThe fix is minimal and focused: it simply reconstructs the `--ci` flag by checking the raw command line arguments and passing it through to the subprocess.\n\n### Testing\nCreated `packages/frai-cli/src/index.test.ts` to verify:\n1. Test starts by confirming the bug exists (test fails with the original code)\n2. After the fix, the test passes, confirming both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are created\n3. Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and verified manually that the workflow is now created correctly\n\nThe package has been rebuilt and all tests pass. The fix is production-ready.",
